 "cards": [
  {
   "key": "whats_going_on",
   "title": "What's going on in the body",
   "text": "Parkinson's (late-onset) is linked to changes in a gene called GBA1, according to HPO [Ede2b693]. A paper reports that mutations in the GBA1 gene lead to reduced activity of the enzyme it makes, called glucocerebrosidase, which cells use to break down and recycle material [Ea15cf24]. A paper reports that this lower enzyme activity lets certain fatty substances build up inside cells and can lead to toxicity and inflammation [E2361d59]. A paper reports that this is tied to a problem in the cell's own cleanup and recycling system, called autophagy, along with other cell functions [E0cfd565]. A paper reports that problems were also seen in mitochondria, the tiny parts of cells that make energy, including changed distribution and function [Ef38c307, E993affc]. A paper reports that these changes disrupt enzyme activity and cause lysosomal (cell cleanup system) problems that lead to higher levels of a protein called alpha-synuclein [Ec7726e8].",
   "citations": [
    "Ede2b693",
    "Ea15cf24",
    "E2361d59",
    "E0cfd565",
    "Ef38c307",
    "E993affc",
    "Ec7726e8"
   ],
   "status": "ok"
  },
  {
   "key": "similar",
   "title": "Diseases that share the same biology",
   "text": "A paper reports that Parkinson's (late-onset) and Gaucher disease are both caused by changes in the same gene, GBA1 [Ea15cf24, Ed85e96b]. A paper reports that both conditions involve a problem called lysosomal enzyme deficiency, where a cell's cleanup enzyme does not work well enough [Ece278e5, E309fa8a]. A paper reports that both also involve a buildup of fatty molecules called glycosphingolipids inside cells, a mechanism called glycosphingolipid storage [E8b12886, Ec8d1187]. According to Reactome, the GBA1 gene takes part in a glycosphingolipid breakdown pathway that is also used by the genes behind Fabry disease, Krabbe disease, GM2 AB variant, and Niemann-Pick A, even though each of these conditions is caused by its own different gene [E8a2d502, Eaeb2dd9, E6be1459, Ee27a382, Eacfbed3]. A paper reports that Fabry disease also involves lysosomal enzyme deficiency, caused instead by changes in a different gene called GLA [E4b5796e, Ebeec4d7]. A paper reports that Krabbe disease also involves lysosomal enzyme deficiency caused by changes in a gene called GALC [E60744b8]. According to HPO, Parkinson's (late-onset) and Fabry disease can both involve abnormal autonomic nervous system physiology, meaning problems with body functions that happen automatically [E7ecf4f2, Ec2b1c5e]. According to HPO, Parkinson's (late-onset) and GM2 AB variant can both include dementia and dystonia [Ed890387, E1ec9ee3, Ea493fb5, E07d362c]. According to HPO, Parkinson's (late-onset) and Niemann-Pick A can both include rigidity and constipation [Ea566976, E1de711d, E61ae178, E02e46a6].",
