  {
   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "Groups, studies and trials that exist",
   "text": "A paper reports that the Silverstein Foundation for Parkinson's with GBA seeks new treatment approaches for Parkinson's disease in people who carry GBA mutations [Ea3b320e]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Prevail Therapeutics runs a trial called PROPEL testing a therapy named LY3884961, along with methylprednisolone and sirolimus, for people with Parkinson's disease who have at least one GBA1 gene change, with sites in Israel and the United States, though it is active but not currently recruiting [E54173b0, E709971f, E99d93eb, E840bf28, Ee4dc801, E9a1447d, Efced915]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Bial R&D Investments ran a compassionate use trial of BIA 28-6156 for people with Parkinson's disease who carry a GBA1 variant, with sites in Spain, the United Kingdom, Italy, Portugal, and the United States, though it is no longer available [Eff10cb4, E634914c, Eee1d4d7, E09720eb, Ee304b33, E0e0a228, E2f615a3, E89ac436]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, the National Human Genome Research Institute runs a completed imaging study and a genetic study of lysosomal storage disorders connected to Parkinson's (late-onset) [Eebd6e8b, E38e3af2, E4f58b66, Eb944295]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, the Pacific Parkinson's Research Centre ran a completed study called the GBA Multimodal Study in Parkinson's Disease, with sites in Canada and the United States [E0fab56b, E8433915, E0b7c828, E45748b0]. According to NIH RePORTER, NIH NINDS funds a grant about restoring GBA1 function in Parkinson disease and Lewy body dementia [Ef68f7ec, Eed2a9bc]. A paper reports that patient groups already exist for related diseases, including the MPS Society in the United Kingdom for Gaucher disease, the Canadian Fabry Association for Fabry disease, and KrabbeConnect in the United States for Krabbe disease [E040d968, E6e80d7b, E7aa1953].",
